{"lines":[{"x":0.090349074590712397,"y":0.045058139716286361,"w":0.059548257191975901,"t":"Test 3","c":1,"h":0.014534883302221635},{"h":0.014749262536873142,"x":0.088295691281104968,"y":0.092920353715730486,"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","w":0.31006159464518229},{"w":0.82751541137695317,"x":0.088295682662212868,"h":0.020470604010387805,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","y":0.12790697655083316,"c":1},{"w":0.17043121337890624,"h":0.016050970589516766,"c":1,"x":0.088295686820921121,"t":"Passage 2 below.","y":0.14825581405931854},{"w":0.51950719197591144,"c":1,"t":"The global importance of wetlands","x":0.24845995626780146,"h":0.024829354750371624,"y":0.1917404125555372},{"c":1,"t":"Wetlands are areas where water covers the soil, or is present either at or near the surface","x":0.1170431137357959,"w":0.77002054850260415,"y":0.23392330371478176,"h":0.016076696165191806},{"h":0.019026548672566257,"t":"of the soil, for all or part of the year. These are complex ecosystems, rich in unique plant","x":0.1334702372052351,"c":1,"y":0.25000000049401394,"w":0.75975357055664061},{"x":0.13347023694396948,"h":0.017535329498020946,"w":0.75154001871744791,"c":1,"t":"and animal life. But according to the World Wide Fund for Nature (WWFN), half of the","y":0.26889534886081368},{"t":"world's wetlands have disappeared since 1990 - converted or destroyed for commercial","x":0.13347023685830331,"h":0.017497598878753573,"w":0.75154001871744791,"c":1,"y":0.28633720932178641},{"h":0.024046186148944493,"y":0.30143593320226203,"t":"development, drainage schemes and the extraction of minerals and peaằMany of those that","c":1,"w":0.79081008911132811,"x":0.13335858728741545},{"t":"remain have been damaged by agricultural pesticides and fertilisers, industrial pollutants,","y":0.32267441862795176,"w":0.76386037190755207,"h":0.017443575338628059,"x":0.13347022461239172,"c":1},{"h":0.017499923706054688,"c":1,"w":0.21015804290771484,"t":"and construction works.","x":0.13317398363053939,"y":0.33875450994688738},{"w":0.75770019531249999,"x":0.1334702307651916,"c":1,"y":0.37640117987303379,"t":"Throughout history, humans have gathered around wetlands, and their fertile ecosystems","h":0.01604068047177476},{"t":"have played an important part in human development. Consequently, they are of","x":0.13141683418121375,"y":0.39380530971904237,"h":0.016224188790560423,"c":1,"w":0.68993840535481765},{"y":0.40967622370317014,"w":0.75169174194335953,"c":1,"t":"considerable religious, historical and archacological value to many communities around","h":0.019768572556937425,"x":0.13339278634681656},{"c":1,"x":0.13341702613475925,"w":0.77836461385091149,"y":0.42730867972512621,"h":0.020450193692097551,"t":"the world. 'Wetlands directly support the livelihoods and well-being of millions of people,'"},{"h":0.017495883952903135,"x":0.13347021928521977,"y":0.44622093024694243,"w":0.78644765218098966,"t":"says Dr Matthew McCartney, principal researcher and hydrologist at the International Water","c":1},{"h":0.020960002662861243,"c":1,"x":0.13338306361231256,"w":0.78045628865559902,"y":0.46235909601109226,"t":"Management Institute (IWMI). 'In many developing countries, large numbers of people are"},{"y":0.48054764594053445,"w":0.47662251790364585,"t":"dependent on wetland agriculture for their livelihoods.'","h":0.01891254661357511,"x":0.13337194180317055,"c":1},{"h":0.017479591032045105,"w":0.71663243611653649,"x":0.13347023087396992,"c":1,"y":0.51740412969759952,"t":"They also serve a crucial environmental purpose. 'Wetlands are one of the key tools"},{"c":1,"t":"in mitigating climate change across the planet,' says Pieter van Eijk, head of Climate","y":0.53480825949984379,"w":0.7268993631998697,"h":0.017517321651312479,"x":0.13141684904688228},{"t":"Adaptation at Wetlands International (WI), pointing to their use as buffers that protect","x":0.13347023634734911,"y":0.5536873157219111,"w":0.73511291503906251,"h":0.016224188790560534,"c":1},{"h":0.014749262536873142,"c":1,"w":0.71457906087239587,"t":"coastal areas from sea-level rise and extreme weather events such as hurricanes and","y":0.57109144566066594,"x":0.13347022304908127},{"h":0.016224188790560534,"y":0.58997050148549701,"c":1,"x":0.13347021792114655,"t":"flooding. Wetland coastal forests provide food and water, as well as shelter from storms,","w":0.75359344482421875},{"y":0.60755813965034178,"t":"and WI and other agencies are working to restore those forests which have been lost. 'It can","c":1,"x":0.13141684989598096,"h":0.01604068047177476,"w":0.78439422607421871},{"c":1,"t":"be as simple as planting a few trees per hectare to create shade and substantially change a","w":0.7639916992187501,"y":0.62436759775761852,"h":0.018323819545869591,"x":0.13339387134349295},{"w":0.78644765218098966,"c":1,"y":0.64098837258731467,"h":0.018895347842776355,"t":"microclimate,' he says. 'Implementing climate change projects isn't so much about money.'","x":0.13141683090946069},{"y":0.67876106203628073,"x":0.13141683036540816,"w":0.77002054850260426,"c":1,"h":0.016006379704208151,"t":"The world's wetlands are, unfortunately, rich sources for in-demand commodities, such as"},{"c":1,"y":0.69616519188178172,"w":0.75975357055664061,"h":0.016044110323475524,"t":"palm oil and pulpwood. Peatlands - wetlands with a waterlogged organic soil layer - are","x":0.13141684910342558},{"t":"particularly targeted. When peatlands are drained for cultivation, they become net carbon","x":0.1334082338996932,"w":0.76192713419596347,"c":1,"h":0.019339451747657943,"y":0.71234650371077735},{"t":"emitters instead of active carbon stores, and, according to Marcel Silvius, head of Climate-","x":0.13340640681289501,"y":0.73077161623922904,"w":0.77630091349283847,"h":0.019616915272400393,"c":1},{"w":0.77217051188151054,"h":0.018848175003816969,"x":0.13137089871433355,"y":0.74835842021168153,"c":1,"t":"smart Land-use at WI, this practice causes six per cent of all global carbon emissions. The"},{"y":0.76744186058031572,"w":0.78234085083007809,"c":1,"h":0.016038965545924433,"x":0.13141684345671631,"t":"clearance of peatlands for planting also increases the risk of forest fires, which release huge"},{"w":0.73921971638997397,"y":0.78488372095323045,"h":0.017476161180344341,"c":1,"t":"amounts of CO2. 'We're seeing huge peatland forests with extremely high biodiversity","x":0.13141683574863805},{"h":0.017441860412777621,"w":0.59958933512369783,"x":0.13141683129412057,"c":1,"t":"value being lost for a few decades of oil palm revenues,' says Silvius.","y":0.80232558141736543},{"t":"* peat: a brown deposit formed by the partial decomposition of vegetation in wet acidic conditions, often cut out and dried for use as fuel","h":0.012774771856347344,"w":0.81115636189778662,"y":0.89533748205949371,"c":1,"x":0.08825421505706979},{"t":"66","w":0.026694043477376306,"h":0.013081394746943587,"y":0.91860465140427661,"x":0.086242300540572636,"c":1},{"t":"IELTSXpress.com","h":0.04166666666666663,"c":1,"x":0.51176470218665204,"w":0.45294118245442705,"y":0.94166666659226195}],"w":2400,"h":3390}